  "id": "COMPOUND:43848 - PROTEIN:6231",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex relationship between the compound (9R,10R,13R,17R)-17-[(2R,5S)-5-hydroperoxy-5-propan-2-ylhept-6-en-2-yl]-10,13-dimethyl-1,2,9,11,12,15,16,17-octahydrocyclopenta[a]phenanthren-3-one and the histone methyltransferase H3 lysine-9 specific 5. This compound is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including (+)-Phylliroside, quillaic acid alpha-L-Arap-(1->4)-alpha-L-Arap-(1->3)-beta-D-Xylp-(1->4)-alpha-L-Rhap-(1->2)-beta-D-fucopyranosyl ester, and Dimethyl 3-hydroxyphthalate. All of these compounds are known to interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is a key component of the polycomb repressive complex 2 (PRC2) and is involved in the methylation of histone H3 lysine 9 (H3K9). This indicates that the compound may act as a modulator or inhibitor of the PRC2 complex, thereby influencing the methylation of H3K9. The evidence suggests that the compound may function as a potential therapeutic agent targeting the H3K9 methyltransferase activity, though the exact mechanism of action and the strength of the interaction remain to be fully elucidated.",
